<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Touba</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Touba is a city in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a>, founded in 1887 by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sufism">Sufi</a> leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amadou-bamba">Amadou Bamba</a> in the former kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baol">Baol</a>. It is the holy city of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mouride-brotherhood">Mouride brotherhood</a> and the site of its Great Mosque, inaugurated in 1963, where Bamba is buried. Each year the Grand Magal pilgrimage brings vast numbers of visitors, and the city has grown into one of the largest in Senegal.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/touba.jpg" alt="Touba" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Crane from Prague, Czech Republic · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Touba_034_(45718877585).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
